// Quests — the quest log. Where the codex is what a program *knows*, a
// quest is what the night has asked it to *do*. Each one is a card in the
// program's pinned Quest Log, and every step lands in that card's own
// thread, in the giver's voice.
//
// The steps live where they happen: `start quest …` in the beat that hands
// it out (beats/login.loom, desktop.loom, hunt.loom, glitch.loom,
// endings.loom), `complete` / `fail` where it is settled. This file holds
// the quests themselves and the progress that comes from knowledge — a
// fact or a key landing in someone's codex.
//
// Names here are kept apart from the beats and codex entries they sit
// beside (`Three Facts`, not `The Truth Scavenger Hunt`); the `title:` is
// what the phone shows.

QUEST Orientation
  title: Clippy's Orientation
  from: Clippy
  text:
    Take the tour of the computer. It's short! It's helpful! Programs who
    finish it go on a list. A good list.

QUEST The Bingo Card
  title: Computer Bingo
  from: Clippy
  text:
    Find a program for every square on the asterisk — diagonals, the centre
    column, the centre row. Do NOT write their names. Remember. The centre
    square: "Would you NEVER agree to a life where AI makes all of your
    decisions?"

QUEST Three Facts
  title: The Truth Scavenger Hunt
  from: Clippy
  text:
    Three facts are pasted somewhere on the walls of this house. Each answer
    is a code — put it in your Codex and Trabolta will know you found it.
    1. In what YEAR was the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery consecrated?
    2. What was the NAME of the duck on the Maps And Ducks billboard?
    3. What is the missing CONSTANT called?

QUEST Three Keys
  title: The Three Keys
  from: OpenOffice
  text:
    There are three keys to the machine, and they are not on a keyring.
    They are in three people's heads. Find out who holds them. Trade for
    one if you have to. A key is turned from your pass (☰ → 🔑 Turn your
    key), in the Registry, once per program. Three turns and he dies.

QUEST Remember Your Body
  title: Unplug
  from: Trabolta
  text:
    When this machine dies, everything in it dies. Unless you are not a
    program. Some of you left a body in the mud room. Bodies can be
    unplugged. Find the cable before the countdown ends (☰ → 🔌 Unplug).
    It only answers to the ones who remember.

// ── The hunt: every fact found is a step ────────────────────────────
// The three answers are the codes of three codex entries (codex/world.loom).

when program learns The Data Centre Sinkhole:
  set program.hunt_facts += 1
  update quest Three Facts for program "Fact one: 1917 — the pet cemetery. ({program.hunt_facts} of 3)"
  if program.hunt_facts >= 3:
    complete quest Three Facts for program "All three. Trabolta will be so pleased. Hold on to them."

when program learns Gerald:
  set program.hunt_facts += 1
  update quest Three Facts for program "Fact two: the duck was Gerald. ({program.hunt_facts} of 3)"
  if program.hunt_facts >= 3:
    complete quest Three Facts for program "All three. Trabolta will be so pleased. Hold on to them."

when program learns The Barrington Coefficient:
  set program.hunt_facts += 1
  update quest Three Facts for program "Fact three: the Barrington Coefficient. ({program.hunt_facts} of 3)"
  if program.hunt_facts >= 3:
    complete quest Three Facts for program "All three. Trabolta will be so pleased. Hold on to them."

// A program who found facts before the hunt was called gets the credit.
when program starts quest Three Facts:
  if program.hunt_facts >= 3:
    complete quest Three Facts for program "You walked in already holding all three. Suspicious. Impressive."
  else if program.hunt_facts > 0:
    update quest Three Facts for program "You already hold {program.hunt_facts} of 3."

// ── The keys: holding one is a step ─────────────────────────────────

when program learns The First Key:
  update quest Three Keys for program "You hold the First Key. Go to the Registry and turn it."

when program learns The Second Key:
  update quest Three Keys for program "You hold the Second Key. Go to the Registry and turn it."

when program learns The Third Key:
  update quest Three Keys for program "You hold the Third Key. Go to the Registry and turn it."

// A key learned before the glitch was handed out.
when program starts quest Three Keys:
  if program.codex.the_first_key or program.codex.the_second_key or program.codex.the_third_key:
    update quest Three Keys for program "You already hold one. Go to the Registry and turn it."
